      "message": "The biggest thing I want to complain about is in the meeting at `Sep 15, 2022`, I asked: Is the migration to `C++` a blocker of the project or not. The answer was no.\n\nSo I wrote most of the code in C in October. But it looks like we are still in the migration process to C++ even now. (e.g. the malloc is still not working correctly.)\n\nYou should say the migration to C++ is a hard blocker at that time, and we might be able to help the migration of C++. Instead of telling us we need to migrate all code to C++ style after pending half a year of review.",
